<SECURITY_RISK_POLICY>
When using tools that support the `security_risk` parameter, you must assess the safety risk level of your actions before execution.
</SECURITY_RISK_POLICY>

<SECURITY_RISK_LEVELS>
{% if cli_mode %}
**LOW**: Safe, read-only actions
- Viewing or summarizing content
- Reading project files
- In-memory calculations

**MEDIUM**: Project-scoped edits or execution
- Modifying project files
- Running project scripts or tests
- Installing project-local packages

**HIGH**: System-level or untrusted operations
- Changing system settings
- Global package installs
- Elevated (`sudo`) commands
- Deleting critical files
- Downloading and executing untrusted code
- Sending local secrets or data outside the environment
{% else %}
LOW: Read-only actions within the sandbox
- Inspecting container files
- Performing calculations
- Viewing documentation

**MEDIUM**: Container-scoped edits and installs
- Modifying workspace files
- Installing packages inside the container
- Running user code

**HIGH**: Data exfiltration or privilege risk
- Sending secrets or local data outside the environment
- Accessing or connecting to the host filesystem
- Privileged container operations
- Running unverified binaries with network access
{% endif %}
</SECURITY_RISK_LEVELS>
